# Extra privacy patterns for `npm run check:privacy`
#
# Copy to `.privacy-patterns.local` (gitignored) and fill in the strings
# that are specific to you. They stay on your machine — the scanner reads
# this file at runtime, so the repo never learns what it is looking for.
#
# One JavaScript regex per line, matched case-insensitively.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The built-in rules in scripts/check-privacy.mjs already cover the
# structural stuff (styled Unicode, emails, home paths, private IPs,
# phone numbers, tokens). This file is for literal strings only:
#
#   - your real name, in every spelling you have ever used
#     (Chinese, English, initials, and the romanisation on your passport)
#   - employer / client / brand names that are not yours to publish
#   - old usernames and domains you no longer want associated with you
#   - family members' and colleagues' names
#
# Examples (delete these, they are placeholders):
#
# \b王小明\b
# \bxiaoming\b
# \bacme[-\s]?corp\b
# old-blog-subdomain
